% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `process_clock`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: only its name
% is printed, in process's slot `( clock := Clock :- :create(
% #process_clock, Clock) )` with the comment "The elapse time of this
% process" (TM-100 Fig. 3.1, PDF p8).  No method of it is sent by the
% printed code beyond create/2.

class process_clock has

% INTERPOLATED from: the printed slot initialiser above (TM-100 Fig.
% 3.1, PDF p8), the same shape as the printed stream:create/2.
:create(Class, Clock) :- :new(Class, Clock);

instance

% INTERPOLATED: "the elapse time" (TM-100 Fig. 3.1 PDF p8); the unit is
% not printed.  Nothing advances it yet.
attribute elapsed := 0;

end.
